1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,850
Finance wants cost, Marketing wants speed.

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:05,600
They disagree.

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,200
You panic and think they hate you.

4
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:09,800
They don't.

5
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:12,737
That friction isn't personal rejection.

6
00:00:12,737 --> 00:00:15,112
It's just role conflict.

7
00:00:15,112 --> 00:00:19,537
Finance is paid to cut costs; Marketing is paid to grow.

8
00:00:19,537 --> 00:00:24,425
If you try to please both, you burn out trying to control the uncontrollable.

9
00:00:24,425 --> 00:00:26,375
The Stoic move?

10
00:00:26,375 --> 00:00:28,675
Stop apologizing.

11
00:00:28,675 --> 00:00:30,962
Stop over-explaining.

12
00:00:30,962 --> 00:00:35,825
Your job is to do the right thing for your role, not to be everyone's friend.

13
00:00:35,825 --> 00:00:39,712
When you stop seeking validation, you gain respect.

14
00:00:39,712 --> 00:00:45,412
Your leaders will say, 'We need more people like him,' even if you never asked for the spotlight.

15
00:00:45,412 --> 00:00:48,100
Calm isn't avoiding conflict.

16
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:51,112
It's knowing the disagreement isn't about you.

17
00:00:51,112 --> 00:00:53,050
It's about the job.

18
00:00:53,050 --> 00:00:56,100
Where do you feel this approval pressure most?

19
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:57,800
Tell me below.

20
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:03,212
Subscribe to @stoic-modernized for practical Stoic tools you can use at work.

